ITEMS = ((('what is anaphylaxis and how it happens', 'how do i recognise anaphylaxis', 'what are the signs of anaphylaxis', 'what does anaphylaxis look like', 'how can i tell if it is anaphylaxis in anaphylaxis', 'what symptoms occur in anaphylaxis', 'how to spot severe anaphylaxis', 'what should i look for in anaphylaxis', 'how do i know if a reaction is anaphylaxis', 'what early signs of anaphylaxis are'), 'Anaphylaxis is a severe allergic reaction that can affect breathing and blood pressure. Signs may include swelling of the lips or tongue, difficulty breathing, wheeze, dizziness, vomiting or collapse. Call emergency services immediately.'), (('what immediate action helps anaphylaxis', 'how do i treat anaphylaxis', 'what is the first aid for anaphylaxis', 'how to respond to anaphylaxis', 'what to do immediately in anaphylaxis', 'how do you handle anaphylaxis', 'which medicine helps in anaphylaxis', 'how can i assist with anaphylaxis', 'what is the best response to anaphylaxis', 'how should i care for anaphylaxis'), 'For anaphylaxis, call emergency services first and help the person use their prescribed adrenaline injector if they have one. Keep them still and comfortable, and do not give food or drink. Stay with them until help arrives.'), (('how do i use an adrenaline injector for anaphylaxis', 'where do i inject for anaphylaxis', 'what is an auto injector for anaphylaxis', 'should i help someone use their injector in anaphylaxis', 'what if i am trained to give an injection in anaphylaxis', 'how many doses are needed in anaphylaxis', 'what if the injector is not available in anaphylaxis', 'how to check an injector is in date in anaphylaxis', 'what to tell the operator about an injector in anaphylaxis', 'who can give adrenaline for anaphylaxis'), 'Use only the injector prescribed to the person and follow its instructions, usually into the outer thigh. Call emergency services even if symptoms improve. A second dose may be needed if advised, and a qualified crew will take over.'), (('what position is best for anaphylaxis', 'should i lay someone down in anaphylaxis', 'how to sit a person with anaphylaxis', 'what if breathing is hard during anaphylaxis', 'should i raise the legs in anaphylaxis', 'what if the person feels faint in anaphylaxis', 'how to keep someone still with anaphylaxis', 'what if they vomit during anaphylaxis', 'how to support the airway in anaphylaxis', 'who can advise about position in anaphylaxis'), 'Let the person rest in the position that eases breathing, often sitting upright, and lie them down with legs raised if they feel faint. If vomiting occurs, turn them on their side. Call emergency services.'), (('what triggers anaphylaxis', 'can food cause anaphylaxis', 'which insect stings lead to anaphylaxis', 'can medicines trigger anaphylaxis', 'does latex cause anaphylaxis', 'what if the trigger is unknown in anaphylaxis', 'how to avoid known allergens in anaphylaxis', 'can exercise trigger anaphylaxis', 'when to see a specialist about triggers in anaphylaxis', 'who can investigate anaphylaxis causes'), 'Anaphylaxis can follow foods, insect stings, medicines or latex, though sometimes the trigger is unclear. Avoid known allergens and carry prescribed treatment if advised. Ask a specialist to investigate if the cause is not known.'), (('what if symptoms return after anaphylaxis', 'can anaphylaxis happen again later', 'what is a biphasic reaction in anaphylaxis', 'how long to watch after anaphylaxis', 'what if swelling comes back in anaphylaxis', 'should i stay with someone after anaphylaxis', 'when to use a second injector in anaphylaxis', 'what if breathing worsens again in anaphylaxis', 'when to call emergency services again in anaphylaxis', 'who can review after anaphylaxis'), 'Symptoms can sometimes return hours after the first episode, so hospital assessment is important even after improvement. Stay with the person and call emergency services if breathing or swelling worsens. Follow any action plan they have.'), (('can anaphylaxis happen without a rash', 'what if there is no swelling in anaphylaxis', 'how to recognise atypical anaphylaxis', 'what if symptoms are only dizziness in anaphylaxis', 'can a reaction start slowly in anaphylaxis', 'what if a child cannot describe symptoms in anaphylaxis', 'how to judge a possible reaction in anaphylaxis', 'what if i am unsure about anaphylaxis', 'when to treat symptoms as serious in anaphylaxis', 'who can confirm an allergy in anaphylaxis'), 'Anaphylaxis can occur without an obvious rash, sometimes with collapse or breathing problems alone. If you suspect a severe reaction, call emergency services rather than waiting for more signs. A specialist can confirm the allergy later.'), (('what to do if someone collapses from anaphylaxis', 'should i start cpr for anaphylaxis', 'what if breathing stops during a reaction in anaphylaxis', 'how to check a pulse in anaphylaxis', 'what if the person is unresponsive in anaphylaxis', 'should i use the injector before cpr in anaphylaxis', 'how to hand over to paramedics in anaphylaxis', 'what to tell the crew about the reaction in anaphylaxis', 'how long to continue cpr in anaphylaxis', 'which paramedic takes over after anaphylaxis'), 'If someone collapses and is not breathing normally, call emergency services and start CPR, using their prescribed injector if available. Tell the crew what triggered the reaction and when. Continue until a qualified person takes over.'), (('how can i prevent anaphylaxis', 'what should people with allergies carry in anaphylaxis', 'how to read food labels for allergens in anaphylaxis', 'should i wear a medical alert in anaphylaxis', 'how to plan for a reaction at school in anaphylaxis', 'what if eating out with an allergy in anaphylaxis', 'how to store an adrenaline injector in anaphylaxis', 'when to review an action plan in anaphylaxis', 'who can help with allergy planning in anaphylaxis', 'what to do after a near miss in anaphylaxis'), 'People at risk should carry prescribed adrenaline and follow an agreed action plan. Check labels and ask about ingredients when eating out. Ask a doctor or allergy nurse to review the plan regularly.'), (('which mistakes to avoid in anaphylaxis', 'should i give water for a reaction in anaphylaxis', 'can i give tablets for anaphylaxis', 'should i let the person stand in anaphylaxis', 'what if i want to wait and see in anaphylaxis', "can i use someone else's injector in anaphylaxis", 'should i induce vomiting in anaphylaxis', 'what if i cannot find their medicine in anaphylaxis', 'when to call for help anyway in anaphylaxis', 'who can advise on first aid in anaphylaxis'), "Do not give food, drink or tablets, do not induce vomiting and do not use another person's injector. Call emergency services even if you cannot find their medicine. Stay with the person and keep them calm while waiting."))
